      "side": 1,
      "message": "I looked it up, and there\u0027s this much more information:\n\n```\nValues below “Attack unlikely” indicate the absence of an attacker.\nValues above “Attack is possible” indicate the presence of an attacker.\nIf a device is unable to determine a NADM value, then it shall report\na NADM value of 𝑈𝑛𝑘𝑛𝑜𝑤𝑛 (0xFF).\n```\n\nThere\u0027s a lot of room for the implementer to decide how to set those thresholds.\n\nWould you like that added?",
